# Coding Style

## Linting & Formatting

```bash
# Run lint
{{PACKAGE_MANAGER}} run lint

# Run format
{{PACKAGE_MANAGER}} run format

# Run both before committing
{{PACKAGE_MANAGER}} run lint && {{PACKAGE_MANAGER}} run format
```

## Hard Rules (never bypass)

- Never disable an ESLint rule (`// eslint-disable`)
- Never use `@ts-ignore` or `@ts-nocheck`
- Never commit if lint fails

## Git Hooks (if configured)

- **pre-commit**: runs lint + type-check
- **commit-msg**: validates commit message format

## Commit Message Format

```
<type>(<scope>): <description>

type: feat | fix | docs | refactor | test | chore
scope: module or feature name
description: concise, imperative mood

Examples:
feat(auth): add JWT refresh token
fix(user): null check before accessing email
docs(readme): update setup instructions
```

## IDE Settings

- Indent: **2 spaces**
- Quotes: **single quotes** (JS/TS) or follow project Prettier config
- Semicolons: follow project Prettier config
